# GitHub Workflow

## Branches

- Default base: `main`
- Feature/fix work: short descriptive branches (e.g. `cursor/<topic>-9177` when using Cloud Agents)
- Never force-push `main`; never commit directly to `main` in agent workflows

## Commits

- Use clear, imperative messages: `feat: …`, `fix: …`, `test: …`, `docs: …`, `ci: …`, `refactor: …`
- One logical change per commit when practical
- Do not commit `.env`, credentials, large binaries, or generated secrets

## Pull requests

- Fill `.github/pull_request_template.md` completely
- Link related issues when they exist
- Describe user-visible impact and test evidence (commands + results)
- Keep PRs focused; split unrelated work

## CI gates

Existing workflows under `.github/workflows/`:

- `ci.yml` — verify changes
- `release.yml` — release / deploy path
- `rollback.yml` — rollback path
- `feature.yml` — AI team feature checklist automation (documentation + PR checks)

Agents must not weaken CI to pass. If CI fails, fix the cause or explain the blocker.

## Agent delivery checklist

1. Implement on a feature branch
2. Run relevant tests locally
3. Commit and push (`git push -u origin <branch>`)
4. Open/update PR with the template
5. Ensure CI is green or document failures with root cause
